    9591/    F7B8 :                     	; In a rather overzealous optimisation, this game doesn't check if
    9592/    F7B8 :                     	; the sprite limit has been reached every time it processes a sprite
    9593/    F7B8 :                     	; piece. Naturally, this leads to the 'Sprite_Table' buffer being
    9594/    F7B8 :                     	; overflowed if too many sprites are processed. To mitigate this, the
    9595/    F7B8 :                     	; developers placed an $80 byte large spill buffer after
    9596/    F7B8 :                     	; 'Sprite_Table', to 'catch' the overflow. Unfortunately, this spill
    9597/    F7B8 :                     	; buffer is not big enough to catch all overflow: this oversight is
    9598/    F7B8 :                     	; responsible for the famous 'Ashua' bug. To fix this, we'll just
    9599/    F7B8 :                     	; undo this optimistaion. Sonic 3 & Knuckles undid this optimistaion
    9600/    F7B8 :                     	; too, but heavily optimised the rest of 'BuildSprites' to make up
    9601/    F7B8 :                     	; for it.
